      {
        "id": 228212,
        "name": "aramis",
        "username": "aramis",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-08-02T20:37:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Anubis\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/anubis/48/4949_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Anubis:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It’s an rpg you never really win the only “lose” condition is  dying</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Even dying isn’t always a loss state.</p>\n<p>A good death to a character, one that was meaningful and appropriate, can be a rewarding end.</p>\n<p>The loss conditions are, IMO…</p>\n<p>[list][<em>]being bored.<br>\n[</em>]being frustrated<br>\n[*]being annoyed by the other participants[/list]</p>",
